# Every package's `format` script loads this file explicitly with --ignore-path, because Prettier
# only auto-discovers a .prettierignore in its own CWD and never walks up to the workspace root.
# Keep patterns `**/`-anchored so they match the same way whether Prettier runs from here or from a
# package directory.

**/pnpm-lock.yaml
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.venv/
**/.pnpm-store/

# Generated from contracts/. Rewriting a generator's output is a diff that comes back on the next
# `pnpm codegen`, and `codegen:check` would then fail on a tree nobody edited.
**/generated/
**/_contract/
docs/openapi.yaml

# Prose, wrapped by hand at 100 columns. `docs/protocol.md` is the specification and it is argued
# over line by line; Prettier reflows it to 150 and rewrites its tables, so a one-sentence amendment
# arrives as several hundred lines of churn over text nobody touched. The same habit produced every
# README and this repo's CLAUDE.md.
**/*.md

# The contracts. The ContractKit plugin will happily rewrite these, and the house style here is long
# trailing `#` documentation on a field, which printWidth counts: the formatter then breaks the only
# breakable thing left and a documented enum becomes three lines. These files are the source of the
# types, the schemas and the SDK, so they are read far more often than they are edited, and the prose
# is the part worth keeping.
**/*.ck
